From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sigivb72-netizen <vergilx63@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:50:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] podot: editor: in-process game runs and iPadOS editor
 adaptations

- Play on platforms without game processes (in-process instances): the
  game runs inside the editor process (InProcessGame) and is shown in a
  floating, movable and resizable game window next to the editor, like
  the Android editor's game window (InProcessGameWindow: Stop, Restart,
  Maximize; touch, mouse and keyboard forwarded to the game). The editor
  stays open and usable. The previous mode (editor shuts down while the
  game runs) is kept in EditorNode::run_game_in_process().
- ~EditorNode restores the process-wide state the editor changed (load and
  save callbacks, placeholders, error notifiers, dialog defaults, ...), and
  editor singletons/registries are cleared, so the next instance (a game,
  the editor again, the project manager) starts clean.
- Reuse the Android mobile-editor adaptations on Apple embedded platforms
  (touch actions panel, virtual keyboard spacer, no external file
  manager/terminal/FBX2glTF, no Game workspace, Mobile renderer default,
  compact main menu); main screen indices no longer assume the Game
  workspace exists.
- Save on focus loss by default on iPadOS; Documents as default project
  folder; system document picker for opening files/folders.
- Project manager: warn before opening a project that likely exceeds the
  device memory or free storage (ProjectDeviceLimits).
- Handle low-memory warnings: drop cached previews and warn the user.
- Apple hardware keyboards use the macOS key conventions (Cmd/Option).
